$DIR/main.p:6:12: cannot pass []int{...} to keep, which keeps it after returning
    []int{...} points into the elements of a slice literal, in f's frame. A
    slice literal (at main.p:5) keeps its elements in an array in f's frame, and
    the slice looks at that array. keep stores s in package variable kept
    (main.p:5), so []int{...} would outlive f's frame.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Change keep to take a value or an owner, which it can keep: an owned[T] from
    new, a shared[T], or a library owner such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)
